# SPI target, mode 0, no chip select: full duplex, one byte per shifter
# word. The shifter samples MOSI on each SCLK rise and shifts MISO out
# right after it (mode 0 only needs the next bit before the next rise).
# The lane loads each reply byte from the source stream before its first
# clock and stores each received byte; the transfer is as long as the
# source. The controller must leave at least one SCLK period between bytes
# (the lane needs about ten clocks to load the next reply).
next:   PULL                        # reply byte
        SHIFT                       # load it and start the shifter
        WAIT event:shifter0_done    # eighth SCLK rise
        RD readback:shifter0_rx
        PUSH
        RD readback:stream_bytes_left
        JNZ next
        HALT
